== R13: this machine, and it is NOT the machine the published tables came from ==
   The cross-language crossing table is a table of absolutes, so every slice
   calibrates its own. This container is an Intel Xeon at 2.10 GHz; every other
   figure in this slice's STATE.md was taken on a 2.80 GHz one. Nothing here is
   comparable to those absolutes and the ratios inside this file are the result.
   This slice's own crossing, measured HERE by the unchanged bench:
     -- the crossing itself, same process and build, linkage=shared --
        register-only barrier, to match the rust harness R13 compares against
       forward 0.497 ns   forward+reverse 0.739 ns   reverse alone 0.241 ns
       forward 0.504 ns   forward+reverse 0.764 ns   reverse alone 0.260 ns
       forward 0.522 ns   forward+reverse 0.770 ns   reverse alone 0.248 ns
       forward 0.602 ns   forward+reverse 0.912 ns   reverse alone 0.310 ns
   The rust slice's own crossing benchmark -- what R13 actually asks each slice to
   quote -- COULD NOT BE RUN, and that is a defect in another slice rather than a
   choice here. `ffi/poc/rust/crates/facade/src/generated/core_native.rs` still calls
   `d.skip(wire)`; C24 changed the shared runtime's signature to `skip(tag, wire)`
   and swept the CPP generator's 13 emission sites, and the rust slice's generated
   tree was not regenerated. 20 E0061 errors, so `cargo build --bin bench` fails.
   `poc/rust/**` is not this slice's to write. Logged as C27.

