sink 67240

The boundary arithmetic this arm is measured against. On this machine a forward
crossing is 0.63 ns and a reverse one 0.30 ns, so the deliveries differ by 0.3 ns
(callback) or 0.63 ns (queue) of BOUNDARY per call. Against the CPU column above,
that is the last digit or beyond it. A delta that separates here is therefore NOT
the crossing: it is the delivery's machinery -- a spawned task, a mutex and a
condvar, a wakeup -- or the host thread count, and the `cb x N` control is what
tells those two apart.


== every difference, counted across every configuration it was asked in ==

